Isomorphic Labs is applying frontier AI to help unlock deeper scientific insights, faster breakthroughs, and life-changing medicines with an ambition to solve all disease.

The future is coming. A future enabled and enriched by the incredible power of machine learning. A future in which diseases are curtailed or cured starting with better and faster drug discovery.&nbsp;

Come and be part of an interdisciplinary team driving groundbreaking innovation and play a meaningful role in contributing towards us achieving our ambitious goals, while being a part of an inspiring and collaborative culture.

The world we want tomorrow is the one we’re building today. It starts with the culture at this company. It starts with you.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

About Iso

Isomorphic Labs (IsoLabs) was launched in 2021 to advance human health by building on and beyond the Nobel-winning AlphaFold system. Since then, our interdisciplinary team of drug discovery experts and machine learning specialists has built powerful new predictive and generative AI models that accelerate scientific discovery at digital speed.

Our name comes from the belief that there is an underlying symmetry between biology and information science. By harnessing AI’s powerful capabilities, we can use it to model complex biological phenomena to help design novel molecules, anticipate how drugs will perform and develop innovative medicines to treat and cure some of the world’s most devastating diseases.

We have built a world-leading drug design engine comprising AI models that are capable of working across multiple therapeutic areas and drug modalities. We are continually innovating on model architecture and developing cutting-edge capabilities to advance rational drug design.

Every day, and with each new breakthrough, we’re getting closer to the promise of digital biology, and achieving our ambitious mission to one day solve all disease with the help of AI.

&nbsp;

Your impact&nbsp;

As Principal, Corporate Development, you will serve as the team’s first full-time dedicated leader supporting Isomorphic Labs’ inorganic growth strategy and execution. Reporting to the VP of Corporate Strategy &amp; Development, you will ensure our scientific and AI breakthroughs are paired with rigorous business case development, disciplined opportunity evaluation, and seamless transaction execution.

Working at the centre of a highly collaborative cross-functional team, spanning R&amp;D, Machine Learning, Business Development, Strategy &amp; Operations, Legal, and Finance, you will own the end-to-end lifecycle of corporate transactions that expand our platform capabilities and long-term ecosystem reach. You will apply strong scientific and technical judgment to proactively identify and evaluate emerging opportunities, partner deeply with technical leaders to shape strategic recommendations, and lead high-impact acquisitions, minority investments, and strategic ventures from initial concept through close.

What you will do&nbsp;

• Market landscaping &amp; scientific triage: Proactively map the external landscape across digital biology, biotechnology, and enabling technologies to identify opportunities that accelerate Isomorphic Labs’ long-term roadmap. Act as a rigorous first-pass technical and commercial filter - assessing scientific validity, technological differentiation, and strategic fit early so internal R&amp;D teams focus on the highest-conviction opportunities

• Business partnering &amp; strategic case development: Build and maintain trusted relationships with business partners across Machine Learning, R&amp;D, and Commercial to evaluate complex inorganic opportunities and crystalise clear, objective business cases. Synthesise scientific, technical, and financial considerations into structured executive recommendations (build vs. partner vs. invest/acquire) for the Executive Leadership Team

• Lead end-to-end transaction execution: Proactively self-direct and run corporate deals end-to-end fro

Our Why At Dotmatics&nbsp;

At Dotmatics, a Siemens company,&nbsp; we believe science, data, and decision-making must be deeply intertwined for innovation to thrive. Our Portfolio includes Luma, LumaLab Connect, ELN Platform, Graphpad Prism, Geneious, SnapGene, Protein Metrics, OMIQ, FCS Express, LabArchives, NQuery, EasyPanel, SoftGenetics and Virscidian.

We have a vision for a new Lab of the Future that will change the future of scientific research.

We have created the world’s most comprehensive digital science platform - best-of-breed software applications already used by more than 2 million scientists, together in a single ecosystem united by a powerful, flexible enterprise data platform. This is not flat data buried away in digital graveyards. This is dynamic, multi-dimensional decision-making.

Scientific enterprises need a new level of effectiveness to achieve tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Illness will not wait. The biosphere will not wait. We are tireless in our vision, because the time for innovation is now.

Shaping the Future of Science At Dotmatics&nbsp;

Our global team of more than 800 colleagues are dedicated to supporting our customers in over 180 countries. Together, with our scientific community of users, we accelerate scientific innovation in order to make the world a healthier, cleaner, and safer place to live.

You’ll join a collaborative, global team pushing the boundaries of scientific innovation.&nbsp; Your ideas and efforts will have a tangible impact, accelerating scientific progress and discovery. We offer a dynamic, remote-friendly environment that fosters high integrity and collaboration, empowering you to excel. Dotmatics is a company built by scientists, for scientists. Combined, we are now the world’s largest cloud-based scientific research R&amp;D platform. We need your help to keep growing and pioneering the future.

We are Science Driven. We are Customer Centric. We are Better Together.&nbsp;

What do we need

Are you a recruiter who thrives in high-growth SaaS environments?
We’re looking for an In-House Talent Partner (360 Recruiter) to own end-to-end hiring across Product &amp; Technology, hiring for software engineering positions such as Full-Stack Engineers, DevOps, Product Managers with a scientific/SaaS background through to Test engineering,&nbsp; you may also have experience in other functions as you will need to be comfortable being a flex player, working on other jobs when volume is high. You’ll be the go-to partner for stakeholders , driving fast-paced hiring across the US, UK, EMEA, LATAM and Canadian markets, while influencing leaders and shaping how we hire world-class talent.
You may also have experience in other functions such as GTM (Go To Market/Sales), solutions architects , as you’ll need to be comfortable being a flex player, supporting sourcing &amp; hiring across other business areas when volume is high, supporting with scheduling interviews, running pre-board and on-boarding activities for the team.

This is a team with low ego, we take on all aspects of the hiring process to get roles to a close &amp; support the hiring activities.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The ideal candidate will be on EST time zone&nbsp;

In this role you will get to&nbsp;

• Own Full-Cycle Hiring : Manage/own the entire recruitment process-from intake with hiring managers to offer stage.

• Stakeholder Partnering: Build strong, trusted relationships with leaders and hiring managers, guiding them on market insights, hiring strategies, and best practices.

• Pipeline/Talent Pool Ownership: Drive candidate pipelines through direct sourcing, outreach, referrals, and market mapping-no hand-offs here!!

• High-Volume Execution: Manage multiple requisitions in a fast-paced SaaS environment, balancing speed with quality of hiring process, interviews and hire.

